# A real R0 central joins on its main branch while its real satellite's subhalo is lost: the
# satellite becomes a Type 2 orphan that keeps its clock (from emt_r0_snap32_satellite) and its
# histories (B:322-337); at the last substep its interpolated Mvir is 0 and the gate passes.
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time state.
# Source: R0 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R0/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 6d859a3a2ea422e31ec04a403221d5a477c49f4dfdba303082dc59f1c6003399), Snap_32 rows 15443 (GalaxyIndex 3000057000000068, Type 0) and 15444 (GalaxyIndex 3000057000000071, Type 1).
# SnapNum: the rows store 32; the galaxies' SnapNum 31 is a constructed call-time value (the
# snapshot they arrive from), and the halo snapshot is 32 (Age and ZZ from a scratch restatement
# of SAGE26's time_to_present on the run's a_list, R/src/core_init.c:159-206).
# Converted back to code units: OutflowRate (times deltaT) and TimeOfLast*Merger (divided by
# UnitTime_in_Megayears).
# Histories: every bin holds the output SFR in code units and ColdGas or ColdGas*Sfr*Z as the
# gas samples (plausible, not SAGE26's own bins).
# deltaMvir constructed (central +2% of Mvir, satellite -5% of Mvir).
# Cooling and Heating constructed as 0.
# The output stores no MergTime: galaxy 0's 999.9 is SAGE26's central clock (B:288); galaxy 1's
# is the oracle's return.mergtime of emt_r0_snap32_satellite.
# galaxy 0 (Type 0): infallMvir, infallVvir, infallVmax, infallStellarMass and TimeOfInfall are
# -1, SAGE26's creation sentinels (R/src/model_misc.c:189-193), not the row's 0.0, which the
# HDF5 writer stores for every Type 0 (R/src/io/save_gals_hdf5.c:1011-1016).
# galaxy 1 (Type 1): infallMvir, infallVvir, infallVmax, infallStellarMass and TimeOfInfall are
# the row's raw output values, which the HDF5 writer stores unconverted
# (R/src/io/save_gals_hdf5.c:1005-1010); TimeOfInfall 28.0 is the snapshot number B:311 assigns,
# as a float.
# Reachability: R0-reachable.
# Kind: a source-reviewed TRANSCRIPTION fixture (driver arithmetic of core_build_model.c,
# which no SAGE26 code in the oracle's link anchors).
